course: dictionary
lesson: 10359
title: Trapping: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Trapping is the -ing form of trap. Many words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show which meaning the writer means. «Otters keep warm with thick, air-trapping fur.» Here trapping means holding air in, so the air stays close to the otter's body and keeps it warm.
explain: Read the clues first. In «The hunters were trapping foxes in the forest», the word foxes and the hunters tell you trapping means catching animals. In «trapping the ball», the word ball and a football skill tell you it means stopping it and controlling it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «trapping heat» means keeping heat in, and the sentence still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning. Check the rest of the text too, not just your first guess.
fact: Trapping means catching animals in traps, or keeping someone or something in a place they cannot get out of.
fact: In sport, trapping means stopping a ball and controlling it, for example with your foot.
fact: «The trappings of fame» means the things that go with fame and show it.
fact: «Greenhouse gases are trapping heat in the atmosphere.» Here trapping means keeping heat in.
fact: Trapping can also be a noun for the work of catching animals: fur trapping was a big trade in early Canada and North America.
exercise: «Otters keep warm with thick, air-trapping fur.» What does air-trapping mean here? | Shining brightly in the sun | Blowing air out of the fur | Catching air in a net | *Holding air in so the otter stays warm
exercise: «The hunters were trapping foxes for their fur.» What does trapping mean? | Stopping a ball with the foot | Growing tall in the forest | Keeping the sun out of the room | *Catching animals in traps
exercise: A coach shouts «Good trapping!» after a player stops a fast ball cleanly. What does trapping mean? | Catching animals | Glowing in the dark | Keeping someone in a room | *Stopping the ball and controlling it
test: «Trapping fingers in doors is a common injury.» What does trapping mean here? | Waving them in the air | *Holding fingers in a place they cannot get out of | Stroking them gently | Counting them slowly
test: «The trappings of fame» means what? | Animals caught in traps | Heat kept in the air | *The things that go with fame and show it | The ball stopped on the pitch
exam: What does trapping mean in «a Venus flytrap is a plant trapping insects»? | Setting a light to attract birds | Growing fast in the spring | *Catching and holding insects, as the plant does | Sleeping in the sun
